  "prefLabel": "Pas 204.04 Role of Complainants in Enforcement Hearings",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pas 204.04 Role of Complainants in Enforcement Hearings. Unless called as a witness or granted party or intervenor status, a person who initiates an adjudicative proceeding by complaining to the board about the conduct of person who becomes a party shall have no role in any enforcement hearing.\n\nSource. #8132, eff 7-30-04",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pas100-300.html"
